<title>MOROCCO: Morocco raises some fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Morocco raises some fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco on Tuesday increased prices of diesel, paraffin and industrial fuel by between 4.4 percent and nearly 12 percent.</p>
<p>The energy ministry said the base price of industrial fuel had been set at 1,872.20 dirhams ($215) a tonne, up 11.9 percent from 1,672.83 dirhams.</p>
<p>Diesel would cost 4.75 dirhams a litre, a 4.4 percent increase, while the new base price of paraffin was 3.93 dirhams a litre, a rise of 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>Petrol prices remained unchanged.</p>
<p>The ministry, in a statement on the official news agency MAP, said the increases followed rises of around $3, to $24 a barrel, in crude oil prices during September.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.7)</p>
